            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the quadratic formula on ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "s^2-2s-1=0",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and take the positive root.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $s>0$ be the original side length, in units.\n$$\\begin{align*}(s+1)^2&=2s^2\\\\s^2+2s+1&=2s^2\\\\s^2-2s-1&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nWith $a=1$, $b=-2$ and $c=-1$, the quadratic formula gives\n$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(1)(-1)}}{2(1)}\\\\s&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt8}{2}\\\\s&=1\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $1-\\sqrt2<0$, the original side length is $1+\\sqrt2$ units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
